aggregation

Stages:
$match - filters for data
$group - group documents
$sort - puts documents in a certain order
$limit - set how many documents you want returned
$project - specify which fields to show in documents
$count - return a document showing a value of number of results
$set - update or create nicew fields
$out - create or update a collection to fill with results from pipeline
$search - search documents
$searchMeta - for searching metadata


Example:
db.zips.aggregate([
  {
    $match: { "state": "CA" }
  },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$city",
      totalZips: { $count : { } }
    }
  }
])

db.sightings.aggregate([
  {
    $match: { specifies_common: "Eastern Bluebird" }
  },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$location.coordinates",
      number_of_sightings: { $count : { } }
    }
  }
])


